&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with product management and other engineering teams to design, build, and operate Zuora&#39;s next-generation Revenue product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop highly flexible common components and APIs that enable product customizability and extensibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the design and delivery of significant features or components within the team, from design through production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop application components and services for scale, using modern backend and cloud-native patterns, including microservices, APIs, and event-driven integrations where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the platform needs of other functional areas and provide design and development assistance as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user needs and build products that are intuitive and easy to use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for high-quality software and promote best practices to produce reliable, maintainable, and fault-tolerant systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in and help facilitate design and code reviews, raising the bar on engineering practices, code quality, observability, and testability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor mid-level and junior engineers through pairing, code review, and technical guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify technical debt within your area and propose pragmatic ways to address it alongside feature work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help drive Zuora&#39;s transition to microservices and cloud-based architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/MS/PhD in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or a relevant degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software development experience specializing in enterprise SaaS software.&lt;/li&gt;
