&lt;h2&gt;Company Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zuora is the finance-first monetization platform for the AI era. As companies shift to usage, credits, tokens, and hybrid pricing, Zuora helps them turn that complexity into revenue by connecting pricing, billing, payments, collections, and revenue in one system built for finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zuora is in the middle of the biggest narrative shift in its history: from the company that defined the Subscription Economy to the platform that makes the AI Economy financially possible. AI is forcing every enterprise to rethink how they price, package, bill, and recognize revenue for products that run on tokens, credits, usage, and outcomes. Zuora is positioning itself as the only end-to-end platform built to do that at enterprise scale, connecting pricing through recognized revenue in one system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That story only becomes real in the market if the analysts who shape enterprise buying decisions believe it. Zuora already holds Leader and #1 rankings in recurring billing and revenue recognition: a Leader in the 2025 Gartner Magic Quadrant for Recurring Billing Applications, a Leader in the Forrester Wave for Recurring Billing Solutions, the #1 ranking in IDC&#39;s MarketScape for Enterprise-Focused Subscription and Usage Management Applications, and the #1 score in MGI&#39;s Automated Revenue Management and Agile Billing ratings. That foundation is the leverage point. The next chapter — being recognized as the definitive platform for AI monetization, in a category that analysts are actively still defining — has not been won yet, and it will be won or lost in the next 12–18 months of report cycles, briefings, and strategy days.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is the person who takes that unclaimed ground. You&#39;ll partner with Product, PMM, and executive leadership to translate what Zuora&#39;s platform actually does into the evidence, narrative, and proof points that elevate conversations with Gartner, Forrester, IDC, ISG, and MGI as Zuora evolves from a billing leader to the system finance teams trust to make AI monetization real.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re in the Bay Area, this is a hybrid position with three days per week in Zuora&#39;s Foster City office. If you&#39;re remote, you&#39;ll collaborate virtually with occasional travel for office visits, analyst events, and offsites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define what &quot;AI monetization leadership&quot; means to analysts&lt;/strong&gt; — build the strategy, calendar, and cadence of briefings, inquiries, and submissions that position Zuora as the category leader with Gartner, Forrester, IDC, MGI, and ISG, at the exact moment these firms are deciding how to evaluate AI pricing, billing, and revenue recognition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn product truth into analyst-ready narrative&lt;/strong&gt; — partner with Product and PMM to translate real platform capability (Monetization Catalog, Flexible Commitments, metered entitlements, revenue automation) into the evidence and proof points analysts need to write Zuora into their reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Win the evaluations that matter&lt;/strong&gt; — lead Zuora&#39;s participation in Magic Quadrants, Waves, MarketScapes, and Buyers Guides end to end: RFIs, demos, fact-checks, and the customer references that make the difference between a mention and a Leader placement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the reference bench that proves the story&lt;/strong&gt; — identify and mobilize the customer evidence (from named accounts using Zuora for AI pricing and revenue recognition) that gives analysts and buyers third-party proof, not just vendor claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Close the loop from analyst feedback to action&lt;/strong&gt; — turn what analysts tell you about competitive gaps, market shifts, and buyer concerns into specific recommendations for messaging, launches, and product strategy, and make sure that intelligence actually reaches the people who can act on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make analyst validation work harder across the funnel&lt;/strong&gt; — package analyst insight, quotes, and rankings into assets that sales, marketing, and customer success actually use in deals and campaigns, not just PR headlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Your Experience&lt;/h2&gt;
